Philip Potter <pgp@doc.ic.ac.uk> wrote:
>Side question: What happens if you wish for a corpse that is not 
>normally generated? e.g. vampire corpse, yellow light corpse, energy 
>vortex corpse, iron golem corpse?

Wishing for a corpse of a unique or corpseless monster instead gets you
a corpse of a random corpseful monster appropriate to the level. If the
selected random monster is undead then it will be converted to its
living counterpart first in the usual way; if all possible monsters on
the level are corpseless then you'll get a human corpse. Wishing for a
corpse of a quest guardian, e.g. student, chieftain, etc., gets you a
corpse of the corresponding player monster.

Tins behave almost identically but fall back slightly differently and
also require the contents to be nutritious, so don't bother trying to
wish for a tin of wraith meat.

